Module skeel "Fair Weather" {
  // ── Chapters ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Chapter ch_fair "Fair Weather" when within(party, reach) and firstDay() "There has not been a cloud over the Gannet Reach for a week.".
  Chapter ch_living "Living Things" when secondDay() and hour(clock) >= 6 "The second morning comes up still and bright over the Reach. On the Strand the tide-bell is ringing at the foot of the Slip, and the carts are going out again.".
  Chapter ch_court "The Wreck Court" when thirdDay() and hour(clock) >= 15 "At three the tide turns on the Strand, and in Skeel the shutters go up on the shops, and people put on their black and go down the Drang to the fish cellars, and climb the stair to the net-loft in silence.".
  Chapter ch_ebb "The Third Ebb" when courtDone(reach) and drownedIn(reach) "On the third ebb, in the dark, the Reach gives back what it took.".

  // ── What else is told when the Court rises ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Relation fateTold(entity).
  Entity fate_grace: fact "the grain left". Entity fate_info: fact "the information laid". Entity fate_kerensa: fact "Kerensa".
  Rule fate_grain when courtDone(reach) and graceGrain(reach) and not fateTold(fate_grace) says "One part in eight of the grain stays in the Wreck-House, entered in Constance Ferrar's ledger as a debt of Ferrar and Daughters to the Strangers' Acre. Skeel does not know what to call it. Parson Hosken calls it grace, and is told to stop." { Assert fateTold(fate_grace). }
  Rule fate_info when courtDone(reach) and constanceKnows(constance) and notWreck(reach) and not henderConfessed(hender) and not henderExposed(hender) and not fateTold(fate_info) says "Constance Ferrar does not say anything about the Reeve in the loft. She has her ledger. A month later, in the south, an information is laid before the Admiral's court in her careful hand, and two officers come up the coast road to Skeel in the rain." { Assert fateTold(fate_info). }
  Rule fate_kerensa when courtDone(reach) and kerensaWalked(party) and not fateTold(fate_kerensa) says "Kerensa Brask is not on the packet when it sails. The blue gig is gone from the slip, and nobody saw her take it out." { Assert fateTold(fate_kerensa). Assert kerensaGone(kerensa). Retract at(kerensa, quay). Retract at(kerensa, net_loft). Assert at(kerensa, limbo). }

  // ── Endings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Told when Ferrar's packet sails on the fourth evening, the Court a day behind and the third ebb come and gone, so
  // that what the Court decided can be lived in for a night and a day before it is told. The first that holds is the
  // one told. The Reach goes on after it, and the company can stay, or come back.
  Ending pilots "The Pilots" when packetSailed(reach) and pilotsAgreed(reach) "The Constancy's grain goes down to the quay in the carts it came up in, and is weighed into Ferrar's packet, and then, at Constance Ferrar's word, two-thirds of it is weighed out again onto the quay and carried back up the Drang to the Wreck-House: three years' pilotage, paid in advance, on every Ferrar hull into the Reach. The contract is drawn in the net-loft that evening in Constance Ferrar's hand and witnessed by Parson Hosken, who weeps. It names the pilots of the Reach: Kerensa Brask, Jinny Rowse, and, as master of the station on Inish Gall, Malachy Sennen, who has not been asked and will be furious. Skeel does not know how to feel about any of it. It has never been paid to keep a ship whole. In the Admiral that night they argue about it until two, and somebody starts singing 'The Twelve Gigs', and the whole taproom comes in on the chorus, badly, as if they had all known it all their lives and forgotten that they did.".
  Ending godson "The Godson" when packetSailed(reach) and henderConfessed(hender) "Hender Brask gives the Wreck-House keys to Parson Hosken on the quay, and the book, and his black coat, and goes home and sits in his parlour to wait for the Admiral's officers, who will come for him on the next packet. The grain goes down to the quay for Ferrar's. Skeel watches it go, house by house, in the doorways, and says nothing; there is nothing to say to a winter. At dusk Loveday Kitto lights the Lantern on the Holm, as she has fourteen thousand times, and then, because she cannot help it, rows herself across to the quay in Jinny Rowse's punt and walks up the Drang, slowly, in her good shawl, and knocks at the Reeve's door; and he lets her in.".
  Ending exposed "The Light in the Pulpit" when packetSailed(reach) and henderExposed(hender) "They do not hang him in Skeel. They do not know how. Jack Cawse and two of his brothers walk Hender Brask down the Drang between them to the quay, gently, as if he were drunk, and lock him in the fish cellars among the idle presses until the packet sails, and Constance Ferrar writes out the information against him in her ledger on her knee by the light of the cellar lamp, and has him sign it, and he does. The grain goes down to the quay for Ferrar's. In the night somebody chalks on the charter board by the church door, under NEITHER MAN NOR DOG NOR CAT, the words NOR BOY, and in the morning Parson Hosken, after thinking about it for a long time, leaves it there.".
  Ending living "A Living Thing" when packetSailed(reach) and notWreck(reach) "The grain goes down to the quay in the carts it came up in. Skeel stands in its doorways and watches it go, sack by sack, into Ferrar's packet, and does not help, and does not hinder, and nobody throws anything, quite. Constance Ferrar pays the carters double and nobody refuses it. Hender Brask stands at the Wreck-House door with the book under his arm and checks every sack against it, and signs for it, in the voice he uses for numbers; and in the evening goes up to the church with his rag and his dish of oil and works it into the gilt letters of the charter one by one, NEITHER MAN NOR DOG NOR CAT, as he has done every week of his life. It is a hungry winter on the Reach that year. They say in the Admiral that it was a dog that did it, and laugh, and stop laughing.".
  Ending share "A Stranger's Share" when packetSailed(reach) and wreckDeclared(reach) and (drownedDog(party) or bribed(party)) "Skeel eats that winter. The grain is shared out house by house, two parts in three, and the factor is paid at Martinmas out of the Admiral's third, and the salt company does not come. The Constancy's saint goes up on the Reeve's gable beside the Lady with the Lyre, the girl with the open book, CONSTANT AND TRUE. Loveday Kitto sits in a room at the back of the Admiral, by Mother Jago's charity, and does not go out. Jack Cawse keeps the Lantern. On the first black night of the winter it goes out, and he does not notice. In the spring a man in Skeel who drinks too much tells a stranger in the Admiral about the stranger who was here when the Constancy came in, who walked the Strand like a native, and did the Reeve a service, and was paid for it; and the stranger he is telling it to asks what service, and the man looks at his beer and does not say.".
  Ending away "Wreck, While You Were Away" when packetSailed(reach) and wreckDeclared(reach) and missedCourt(party) "You are not in the net-loft when the Reeve says the word, and you hear it afterward, the way you hear news of a place you have left: from a carter on the coast road, cheerfully, as good news. Wreck, the Constancy, two parts to Skeel. They'll eat this winter on the Reach. The old woman who let the Lantern go out has been turned off, poor soul, and the Reeve's man has it now. The carter flicks his whip. Funny thing, he says: there was a dog.".
  Ending wreck "Wreck" when packetSailed(reach) and wreckDeclared(reach) "Skeel eats that winter. The grain is shared out house by house, two parts in three, and the factor is paid at Martinmas out of the Admiral's third, and the salt company does not come. The Constancy's saint goes up on the Reeve's gable beside the Lady with the Lyre: a girl with an open book, CONSTANT AND TRUE. On the Sunday after, the church of Lir Who Gives sings the Wreck Psalm, IF SHIPS MUST FOUNDER, LORD, SEND THEM TO SKEEL, and Hender Brask stands in the front pew and sings it with the rest, every word, and in the evening oils the charter board. Loveday Kitto is gone off the Holm. Jack Cawse keeps the Lantern now, and is proud of it, and the light goes out across the Reach every night in its long gold road, and nobody on a ship coming in from the south could tell the difference.".
}
